{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>It will please, more than an ox</b> — The mem of משור follows after, as if it were written: משור מפר, like ככבש אלוף (as if) ככבש כאלוף, for the ox is larger than the bull, and how can שור be construct to פר, like: קח את פר השור." "<b>Horned and split-hoofed</b> — It returns to the bull alone, which is seen [to have] its horn and its split hoof. The meaning: that it is not very small."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 69, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra argues the prefixed mem in משור should be understood as if the word is repeated before פר, drawing an analogy to a similar phenomenon he identifies in the phrase ככבש אלוף."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:33:43.774457012Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}